# Business Narrative Standards (LOCKED)

Applies to all work under `business/ADF-v1.0/` from BUSINESS-002 through BUSINESS-011.
Authoritative detail: `business/ADF-v1.0/BUSINESS_RULES.md` (BD-007, BD-008).

## Required

- Professional, diligence-ready prose — not promotional copy
- Capability claims must match BUILD-001 … BUILD-020 (`1.0.0-rc1`) or be labeled roadmap
- Narratives must be suitable for investors, enterprise customers, and government
- Keep positioning consistent with the Executive Package unless a new BD entry supersedes it
- Product editions follow BD-008: useful Community; Pro for software houses/consultants/teams; Enterprise = governance/audit/deployment/support; Cloud = future only

## Forbidden without evidence

- “Best in the world,” “revolutionary,” “number one,” “industry-leading,” and similar hype
- Exaggerated market or technology claims
- Inventing features that are not shipped in RC1
- Presenting Cloud Edition as currently available

## Stop rule

Do not start the next BUSINESS phase unless explicitly instructed.
